# Walkthrough: Dual-Strike Notification System

## Summary
Implemented Expo Push Notifications as an offline safety net alongside the existing Socket.IO system. The system follows a "Dual-Strike" pattern:
- **App OPEN** → Push banners silently suppressed; WebSocket handles everything
- **App CLOSED/BACKGROUNDED** → Push banner appears; tapping routes to the correct screen

**Zero changes** to existing WebSocket logic. All push code is additive.

---

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Backend Trigger Event"] --> B["Socket.IO Emit (existing)"]
    A --> C["Expo Push Send (new)"]
    B --> D{"App State?"}
    C --> D
    D -->|Foreground| E["WebSocket updates UI"]
    D -->|Foreground| F["Traffic Cop MUTES push banner"]
    D -->|Background/Killed| G["OS shows push banner"]
    D -->|Background/Killed| H["WebSocket disconnected"]
    G -->|User taps| I["Deep-link routes to screen"]
```

